# A created object stands above a created object, and both layouts have a slot for `_label`, which the setter of the literal lays late. The slot of the object above is empty when the first object below it is linked.
# The guard "nothing above answers for `_label`" may not begin there, with extra properties on the object above or without: a store in compiled code fills that slot, and a test of the guard that stands in front of the loop is not asked again.
